{"id": "EUVD-2026-78234", "enisaUuid": "ce3bc45d-e614-36fd-9452-9f692ce65d5d", "description": "GNU libextractor before 1.15 contains a stack-based buffer overflow vulnerability in the process_star_office function that sizes a variable-length stack array from attacker-controlled OLE2 stream data. Attackers can craft malicious StarOffice documents that allocate up to 4 MB on the stack, causing stack overflow and crashing any application extracting metadata from the document.", "datePublished": "2026-09-15T00:35:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:22:22", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Haitam-lazaar/libextractor-ole2-rce", "https://git.gnunet.org/gnunet/libextractor/commit/04004eb19033e093938138b09befdf31e71e8522.html", "https://git.gnunet.org/gnunet/libextractor/commit/2781c7e9095f4ddaff4f535d69342f3903b18422.html", "https://www.gnu.org/software/libextractor/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gnu-libextractor-before-1.15-stack-overflow-via-ole2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vrwm-2jf2-f6fv", "CVE-2026-91752"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.74, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2a9ba142-e886-31dc-88aa-d326a0fb833d", "product": {"name": "libextractor", "vendor": {"name": "GNU"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "44024e62-1688-35a1-98cc-22c7d9944827", "vendor": {"name": "GNU"}}], "isExploited": false}